# CACHE RULES. Without these a stale deploy white-screens the game, which is what happened:
# the browser held an index.html from an earlier deploy, asked for a bundle that had since been
# replaced, and got the SPA fallback page instead of JavaScript. Chrome refuses to run HTML as a
# module and the screen stays blank.
#
# The rule is the standard one for hashed builds, and the two halves are opposites on purpose.

# THE HTML MUST NEVER BE CACHED. It is the only file whose name does not change between deploys,
# so a cached copy is a copy pointing at bundles that no longer exist. It is 1 KB; re-fetching it
# costs nothing and is the entire safeguard.
/
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate

# THE BUNDLES CAN BE CACHED FOREVER, precisely because their names contain a content hash. A changed
# file is a different URL, so there is no such thing as a stale one — and caching them hard is what
# makes a repeat visit instant.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
